;==========================================================================
; override.cfg  --  per-car overrides for GP2Lap (pointed to by SeasonOverrides)
;==========================================================================
; Enable by setting, in gp2lap.cfg:
;     SeasonOverrides = "override.cfg"
; If that line is commented out, or this file is missing, the feature is OFF
; and the game behaves stock.
;
; Currently supported override: per-CAR car textures (liveries).
;   carNN = <path to a BMP>
;     NN   = the in-game CAR ID (1..40). The game shows the current car's
;            name (when you switch cars) and number (in the cockpit), so you
;            can confirm which ID is which driver visually.
;     BMP  = a 256 x 164, 8-bit (256-colour) Windows BMP, in the same palette
;            as the car JAM atlases (e.g. exported from GP2Edit). Paths are
;            relative to the GP2 directory; '\' or '/' both work.
;
; A car with NO entry here renders stock (its team livery + its number).
; A bad/missing/wrong-size BMP is skipped (logged) and that car stays stock.
; Lines starting with ';' or '#' are comments. [Sections] are ignored for now.
;==========================================================================

car01 = liv\01a.bmp
car02 = liv\01b.bmp
car03 = liv\02a.bmp
car04 = liv\02b.bmp
; ... add the rest of your grid the same way (car05 = liv\03a.bmp, etc.)
